{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Please take.</b> נָא is nothing but a term of request. He said to him: I ask of you — stand for Me in this trial, so that they should not say of the earlier trials: there was no substance in them." "<b>Your son.</b> He said to Him: I have two sons. He said to him: your only one. He said to Him: this one is the only one to his mother and this one is the only one to his mother. He said to him: whom you love. He said to Him: I love both of them. He said to him: ״אֶת יִצְחָק״ (Sanhedrin 89b). And why did He not reveal it to him at the outset? So as not to confound him suddenly and unsettle his mind over it and drive him mad — and in order to endear the commandment upon him and to give him reward for every word and word." "<b>The land of Moriah.</b> Jerusalem, and so in Chronicles: ״to build the house of Elohim in Jerusalem, on Mount Moriah״ (II Chronicles 3). And our Rabbis explained: so named because from there instruction (הוֹרָאָה) goes forth to Israel. And Onkelos translated it after the incense service, for it contains myrrh, nard, and other spices." "<b>And offer him.</b> He did not say to him: slaughter him — because the Holy One, blessed be He, did not wish to slaughter him but to bring him up the mountain to make of him an offering. And once he had brought him up, He said to him: bring him down." "<b>One of the mountains.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, makes the righteous yearn, and only afterward reveals to them. And all this is in order to multiply their reward. And likewise: ״אֶל הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְאֶךָּ״ (Genesis 12), and likewise in Jonah: ״וּקְרָא עָלֶיהָ אֶת הַקְּרִיאָה״ (Jonah 3:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:56.718228850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}